  "details": "Certain IPA symbols that rely on Unicode combining diacritics are not rendered correctly in profile text. The base character is displayed, but the combining mark is positioned incorrectly.\n\nThis makes some phonetic transcriptions inaccurate or impossible to display as intended.\n\nThe following Unicode IPA sequences do not appear to render correctly:\n\n- ɯ̥ (Voiceless close back unrounded vowel (U+026F + U+0325))\n\n- a̠ (Retracted open vowel (U+0061 + U+0320)), also renders incorrectly on Canny\n\nIn both those cases, the diacritic is rendered to the right of the character instead of below.\n\nThe problematic diacritic symbols seems to be:\n\n- Voiceless ring below (U+0325)\n\n- Retracted diacritic (U+0320)\n\nReference:\n\nhttps://unicodeplus.com/U+0320\n\nhttps://unicodeplus.com/U+0325\n\nTested on PC only, other platforms may also be affected.\n\nSpeculation: This might affect the entire family both these symbols are part of: https://unicodeplus.com/combining/220",
